      ":question/worked-solution": "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot(b\\times c)&=|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 8 & k & 8 \\\\ -3 & 4 & -6\\end{aligned}|\\\\ &=((-4)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & 8 \\\\ 4 & -6\\end{aligned}|)+((-5)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}8 & 8 \\\\ -3 & -6\\end{aligned}|)+((5)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}8 & k \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}|)\\\\ &=((-4)\\cdot ((k)\\cdot (-6)-(8)\\cdot (4)))+((-5)\\cdot ((8)\\cdot (-6)-(8)\\cdot (-3)))+((5)\\cdot ((8)\\cdot (4)-(k)\\cdot (-3)))\\\\ &=((-4)\\cdot (-6k-32))+((-5)\\cdot (-24))+((5)\\cdot (3k+32))\\\\ &=(24k+128)+(120)+(15k+160)\\\\ &=39k+408\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}39k+408&=0\\\\ 39k&=-408\\\\ k&=-\\frac{136}{13}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=-\\frac{136}{13}.$",
