      ":question/worked-solution": "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot(b\\times c)&=|\\begin{aligned}-5 & -8 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 6 \\\\ k & 6 & 5\\end{aligned}|\\\\ &=((-5)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-6 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 5\\end{aligned}|)+((8)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 \\\\ k & 5\\end{aligned}|)+((4)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 \\\\ k & 6\\end{aligned}|)\\\\ &=((-5)\\cdot ((-6)\\cdot (5)-(6)\\cdot (6)))+((8)\\cdot ((2)\\cdot (5)-(6)\\cdot (k)))+((4)\\cdot ((2)\\cdot (6)-(-6)\\cdot (k)))\\\\ &=((-5)\\cdot (-66))+((8)\\cdot (10-6k))+((4)\\cdot (6k+12))\\\\ &=(330)+(80-48k)+(24k+48)\\\\ &=458-24k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}458-24k&=0\\\\ -24k&=-458\\\\ k&=\\frac{229}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=\\frac{229}{12}.$",
