      ],
      ":question/worked-solution": "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot(b\\times c)&=|\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 & -6 \\\\ -5 & -6 & k \\\\ -6 & 5 & 5\\end{aligned}|\\\\ &=((8)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-6 & k \\\\ 5 & 5\\end{aligned}|)+((-4)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-5 & k \\\\ -6 & 5\\end{aligned}|)+((-6)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-5 & -6 \\\\ -6 & 5\\end{aligned}|)\\\\ &=((8)\\cdot ((-6)\\cdot (5)-(k)\\cdot (5)))+((-4)\\cdot ((-5)\\cdot (5)-(k)\\cdot (-6)))+((-6)\\cdot ((-5)\\cdot (5)-(-6)\\cdot (-6)))\\\\ &=((8)\\cdot (-5k-30))+((-4)\\cdot (6k-25))+((-6)\\cdot (-61))\\\\ &=(-40k-240)+(100-24k)+(366)\\\\ &=226-64k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}226-64k&=0\\\\ -64k&=-226\\\\ k&=\\frac{113}{32}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=\\frac{113}{32}.$",
