      ":question/worked-solution": "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot(b\\times c)&=|\\begin{aligned}7 & 8 & 8 \\\\ -8 & k & 8 \\\\ -4 & 5 & 2\\end{aligned}|\\\\ &=((7)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & 8 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}|)+((-8)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-8 & 8 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|)+((8)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-8 & k \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{aligned}|)\\\\ &=((7)\\cdot ((k)\\cdot (2)-(8)\\cdot (5)))+((-8)\\cdot ((-8)\\cdot (2)-(8)\\cdot (-4)))+((8)\\cdot ((-8)\\cdot (5)-(k)\\cdot (-4)))\\\\ &=((7)\\cdot (2k-40))+((-8)\\cdot (16))+((8)\\cdot (4k-40))\\\\ &=(14k-280)+(-128)+(32k-320)\\\\ &=46k-728\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}46k-728&=0\\\\ 46k&=728\\\\ k&=\\frac{364}{23}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=\\frac{364}{23}.$",
