      ":question/worked-solution": "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot(b\\times c)&=|\\begin{aligned}5 & -5 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 3 & -8 \\\\ k & 7 & 7\\end{aligned}|\\\\ &=((5)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & -8 \\\\ 7 & 7\\end{aligned}|)+((5)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & -8 \\\\ k & 7\\end{aligned}|)+((-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ k & 7\\end{aligned}|)\\\\ &=((5)\\cdot ((3)\\cdot (7)-(-8)\\cdot (7)))+((5)\\cdot ((4)\\cdot (7)-(-8)\\cdot (k)))+((-2)\\cdot ((4)\\cdot (7)-(3)\\cdot (k)))\\\\ &=((5)\\cdot (77))+((5)\\cdot (8k+28))+((-2)\\cdot (28-3k))\\\\ &=(385)+(40k+140)+(6k-56)\\\\ &=46k+469\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}46k+469&=0\\\\ 46k&=-469\\\\ k&=-\\frac{469}{46}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=-\\frac{469}{46}.$",
