      ":question/worked-solution": "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot(b\\times c)&=|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 4 & -4 & -7 \\\\ k & -3 & -2\\end{aligned}|\\\\ &=((-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & -7 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}|)+((-4)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & -7 \\\\ k & -2\\end{aligned}|)+((8)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & -4 \\\\ k & -3\\end{aligned}|)\\\\ &=((-3)\\cdot ((-4)\\cdot (-2)-(-7)\\cdot (-3)))+((-4)\\cdot ((4)\\cdot (-2)-(-7)\\cdot (k)))+((8)\\cdot ((4)\\cdot (-3)-(-4)\\cdot (k)))\\\\ &=((-3)\\cdot (-13))+((-4)\\cdot (7k-8))+((8)\\cdot (4k-12))\\\\ &=(39)+(32-28k)+(32k-96)\\\\ &=4k-25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4k-25&=0\\\\ 4k&=25\\\\ k&=\\frac{25}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=\\frac{25}{4}.$",
