      ":question/worked-solution": "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot(b\\times c)&=|\\begin{aligned}4 & -8 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 8 & -5 \\\\ -4 & -8 & k\\end{aligned}|\\\\ &=((4)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}8 & -5 \\\\ -8 & k\\end{aligned}|)+((8)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & -5 \\\\ -4 & k\\end{aligned}|)+((4)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 8 \\\\ -4 & -8\\end{aligned}|)\\\\ &=((4)\\cdot ((8)\\cdot (k)-(-5)\\cdot (-8)))+((8)\\cdot ((5)\\cdot (k)-(-5)\\cdot (-4)))+((4)\\cdot ((5)\\cdot (-8)-(8)\\cdot (-4)))\\\\ &=((4)\\cdot (8k-40))+((8)\\cdot (5k-20))+((4)\\cdot (-8))\\\\ &=(32k-160)+(40k-160)+(-32)\\\\ &=72k-352\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}72k-352&=0\\\\ 72k&=352\\\\ k&=\\frac{44}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=\\frac{44}{9}.$",
