      ":question/worked-solution": "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot(b\\times c)&=|\\begin{aligned}-5 & -6 & -4 \\\\ 6 & k & 2 \\\\ -8 & 6 & -8\\end{aligned}|\\\\ &=((-5)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & 2 \\\\ 6 & -8\\end{aligned}|)+((6)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 \\\\ -8 & -8\\end{aligned}|)+((-4)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}6 & k \\\\ -8 & 6\\end{aligned}|)\\\\ &=((-5)\\cdot ((k)\\cdot (-8)-(2)\\cdot (6)))+((6)\\cdot ((6)\\cdot (-8)-(2)\\cdot (-8)))+((-4)\\cdot ((6)\\cdot (6)-(k)\\cdot (-8)))\\\\ &=((-5)\\cdot (-8k-12))+((6)\\cdot (-32))+((-4)\\cdot (8k+36))\\\\ &=(40k+60)+(-192)+(-32k-144)\\\\ &=8k-276\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8k-276&=0\\\\ 8k&=276\\\\ k&=\\frac{69}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=\\frac{69}{2}.$",
