      ":question/worked-solution": "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot(b\\times c)&=|\\begin{aligned}5 & -5 & 8 \\\\ 8 & -4 & k \\\\ 5 & 3 & 3\\end{aligned}|\\\\ &=((5)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}|)+((5)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}8 & k \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{aligned}|)+((8)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}8 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{aligned}|)\\\\ &=((5)\\cdot ((-4)\\cdot (3)-(k)\\cdot (3)))+((5)\\cdot ((8)\\cdot (3)-(k)\\cdot (5)))+((8)\\cdot ((8)\\cdot (3)-(-4)\\cdot (5)))\\\\ &=((5)\\cdot (-3k-12))+((5)\\cdot (24-5k))+((8)\\cdot (44))\\\\ &=(-15k-60)+(120-25k)+(352)\\\\ &=412-40k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}412-40k&=0\\\\ -40k&=-412\\\\ k&=\\frac{103}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=\\frac{103}{10}.$",
