      ":question/problem": "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=\u27e87,-6,6\u27e9$, $b=\u27e8-3,8,k\u27e9$, and $c=\u27e8-4,-2,-4\u27e9$ are coplanar.\n\n$k=${{field-1}}",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "7b6e6574-5926-58ce-a1f9-b5aac1a5ae6b",
          ":answer-field/key": "field-1",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/blank",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "dbc69c92-3470-5c46-84e6-267ee4608379",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-2"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "dbc69c92-3470-5c46-84e6-267ee4608379"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/worked-solution": "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot(b\\times c)&=|\\begin{aligned}7 & -6 & 6 \\\\ -3 & 8 & k \\\\ -4 & -2 & -4\\end{aligned}|\\\\ &=((7)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}8 & k \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{aligned}|)+((6)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & k \\\\ -4 & -4\\end{aligned}|)+((6)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 8 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}|)\\\\ &=((7)\\cdot ((8)\\cdot (-4)-(k)\\cdot (-2)))+((6)\\cdot ((-3)\\cdot (-4)-(k)\\cdot (-4)))+((6)\\cdot ((-3)\\cdot (-2)-(8)\\cdot (-4)))\\\\ &=((7)\\cdot (2k-32))+((6)\\cdot (4k+12))+((6)\\cdot (38))\\\\ &=(14k-224)+(24k+72)+(228)\\\\ &=38k+76\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}38k+76&=0\\\\ 38k&=-76\\\\ k&=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=-2.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard"
    },
