    "question": {
      ":question/id": "13aa9f7e-7208-591a-aa16-d662a7abf440",
      ":question/problem": "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=\u27e8-8,-8,7\u27e9$, $b=\u27e8k,-4,-7\u27e9$, and $c=\u27e8-8,3,5\u27e9$ are coplanar.\n\n$k=${{field-1}}",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "b7b78496-0d61-530e-aff6-178997cc415d",
          ":answer-field/key": "field-1",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/blank",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "62b9b3e4-dec6-55b6-9bce-5596e27e2be6",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{680}{61}"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "62b9b3e4-dec6-55b6-9bce-5596e27e2be6"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/worked-solution": "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot(b\\times c)&=|\\begin{aligned}-8 & -8 & 7 \\\\ k & -4 & -7 \\\\ -8 & 3 & 5\\end{aligned}|\\\\ &=((-8)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & -7 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}|)+((8)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & -7 \\\\ -8 & 5\\end{aligned}|)+((7)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & -4 \\\\ -8 & 3\\end{aligned}|)\\\\ &=((-8)\\cdot ((-4)\\cdot (5)-(-7)\\cdot (3)))+((8)\\cdot ((k)\\cdot (5)-(-7)\\cdot (-8)))+((7)\\cdot ((k)\\cdot (3)-(-4)\\cdot (-8)))\\\\ &=((-8)\\cdot (1))+((8)\\cdot (5k-56))+((7)\\cdot (3k-32))\\\\ &=(-8)+(40k-448)+(21k-224)\\\\ &=61k-680\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}61k-680&=0\\\\ 61k&=680\\\\ k&=\\frac{680}{61}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=\\frac{680}{61}.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard"
    },
