      ":question/worked-solution": "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot(b\\times c)&=|\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & -8 \\\\ -5 & k & 5 \\\\ 5 & 5 & -5\\end{aligned}|\\\\ &=((4)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ 5 & -5\\end{aligned}|)+((-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-5 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -5\\end{aligned}|)+((-8)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-5 & k \\\\ 5 & 5\\end{aligned}|)\\\\ &=((4)\\cdot ((k)\\cdot (-5)-(5)\\cdot (5)))+((-3)\\cdot ((-5)\\cdot (-5)-(5)\\cdot (5)))+((-8)\\cdot ((-5)\\cdot (5)-(k)\\cdot (5)))\\\\ &=((4)\\cdot (-5k-25))+((-3)\\cdot (0))+((-8)\\cdot (-5k-25))\\\\ &=(-20k-100)+(0)+(40k+200)\\\\ &=20k+100\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20k+100&=0\\\\ 20k&=-100\\\\ k&=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=-5.$",
